Z||000000||kempo||09-27-2001||08:21 PM||||I cannot seem to find much information about these Pace fieros.  So, I'd like for the people who know about them, to educate me about them.  Are they 4 or 6 cylinders and with what displacement?  How many were made?  You know, stuff like that.  Only Automatic, or stick?  0-60mph times, quarter times?  Anybody that knows anything, please educate me!  I really like 'em.  How much could I pick one up for?  Thanks!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.admist.net/kempsig.jpg"> <BR>87 Fiero GT / 5 Speed<BR>86 Fiero 2m4 - FOR SALE||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||09-27-2001||08:39 PM||||There are 2 kinds. The REAL Pace cars and the replica pace cars. The REAL ones are not street legal, and were specially built for the race. They had a 2.7L SD4 engine. (Super Duty 4-cyl) That put out 232hp.<BR>The production replica's are a regular 84 Fiero SE with the 2.5L 4-cyl. The only differences are the appearence stuff. Aero notchback body, red/gray interior, special graphic's, white with silver trim paint, White wheels, special painted air cleaner cover and valve cover, etc.<BR>They only made 2000 of them and 200 were stick the rest were auto's. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||kempo||09-27-2001||08:46 PM||||Is that 2000 OFFICIAL pace cars, or replica's?  And were the real pace fiero's auto?  If I had a real indy pace fiero, I'd drive it on the street- legally or not =)  hehe...||||reg||1
Z||000003||Old Lar||09-27-2001||09:19 PM||||Only four (4) real Pace cars were made.  The 2000 Pace car replicars all had the 2.5 iron duke 4 cylinder engine.  Ya know the one with 92 HP.  The engines that had bad connecting rods.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Frans2..jpg">  <BR>Now this one is a modified Indy Pace Car.  To buy a Pace car replicar, you can pay any where from $500-$20000 depending on condition. New they were $15000.<p>[This message has been edited by Old Lar (edited 09-27-2001).]||||reg||1
